from pathlib import Path
import json,datetime
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def read(name):return json.loads((ROOT/'reports'/name).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
delivery=read('delivery-checks.json');validation=read('validation.json');browser=read('browser.json');long=read('long-record-identification.json')
out='# Audit status\n\nSnapshot: '+datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()+'\n\n'
out+='## Completed work\n\n- Eight original recordings decoded and profiled in full; original hashes verified unchanged.\n- Eight evidence/confidence worksheets, complete tentative bar charts, machine-readable texture timelines, timestamped spectral observations, 16 short source excerpts, and diagnostic probes.\n- Named catalog preview matching where available; long-record recurrence and block-by-block identity investigation.\n- Executable real-Strudel transpiler/REPL/event validator and Chrome WebAudio capture tests.\n- Source/reference comparison tool with an identical-audio calibration control.\n\n'
out+=f'Delivery/control checks: **{sum(x["status"]=="PASSED" for x in delivery)}/{len(delivery)} passed**. These include file presence and integrity; they are not {len(delivery)} album playback tests. One diagnostic is intentionally silent because no valid low-register peaks were detected in its initial 16 seconds.\n\n'
out+='## Long recordings\n\n| Track | Named first cycle | Whole-cycle correlation | Ten-second source blocks matched |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'
for r in long:
 d=json.loads((ROOT/'timelines'/f'{r["track"]}.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));repeat=d['repeat_evidence']
 out+=f'| {d["title"]} | 0–{d["usable_segment"]["end_s"]} s | {repeat["whole_cycle_correlation"]} | {r["matched_blocks"]}/{r["total_blocks"]} |\n'
out+='\nUnmatched blocks are unresolved, not automatically unrelated songs. Some span loop boundaries or edits. Sailor Song has a substantial unresolved region around 1040–1170 s; Love Me Not has one around 1490–1590 s and other edited/transition blocks. Inspect reports/long-record-identification.json before using the tail. Use the first identified cycles for this album.\n\n'
out+='## Technical outcomes\n\n'
for name,data in [('Node Strudel controls',validation),('Browser WebAudio controls',browser)]:out+=f'- {name}: '+', '.join(f'{c.get("id",c.get("name"))}: {c["status"]}' for c in data['selftests'])+'.\n'
control=next(x for x in browser['selftests'] if x['id']=='control-sine')['observed'];out+=f'- Positive audio capture: {control.get("decoded_audio_metrics")}. This is a synthetic control, not a song rendering.\n'
passed_tracks=sum(x['status']=='PASSED' for x in validation['tracks']);out+=f'- Album root inspected: `{validation["album_root"]}`. Strudel syntax/event generation: **{passed_tracks}/{len(validation["tracks"])} playlist arrangements PASSED**.\n'
player=browser.get('player',{});player_passed=sum(x.get('status')=='PASSED' for x in player.get('media',[]));order_passed=sum(x.get('status')=='PASSED' for x in player.get('order',[]));out+=f'- Chrome `file://` page playback: **{player.get("status","PENDING")}**; {player_passed}/{len(player.get("media",[]))} mapped MP3s decoded and advanced; {order_passed}/{len(player.get("order",[]))} Strudel audio declarations matched the player sources. This confirms local offline-file playback in this Chrome run; HTTP hosting was not tested.\n'
out+='- All eight weighted fidelity scores: **PENDING**, numeric score null. Six-second browser captures only establish that the code renders audio; they do not establish resemblance to the recordings.\n\n'
out+='## Musical limits and remaining work\n\nNo critical listening was performed. The available work does not certify exact melody, bass transcription, chord progressions, meter, instrument identity, swing or verse/chorus labels. The supplied candidates are engineering evidence for musician review, not completed faithful-cover specifications. No subjective similarity claim is made.\n\nResolve beat-level ambiguity before using any inferred bar grid. In particular, Can\'t Tell Me Nothing has competing periodicity estimates: about 79.51 BPM in autocorrelation versus 107.67 from the default-prior beat tracker. Its automatic bar chart must not be treated as confirmed. Without Me has close G-minor/G-major profile fits; Everyday Normal Guy 2 has weak/conflicting tonal fits; Love Me Not and Lonely have relative-mode ambiguity.\n\nFor fidelity completion, compare browser-rendered instruments and phrases against the corresponding source excerpts, resolve the listed beat/key ambiguities, and conduct critical listening before filling the rubric. The current browser run is a six-second render, not a likeness test. Read INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md for the concrete per-track priorities.\n'
(ROOT/'reports/AUDIT_STATUS.md').write_text(out,encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote reports/AUDIT_STATUS.md')
